This project uses the Signal design library (`signal-design`). Before writing UI,
read `node_modules/signal-design/AGENTS.md`, and copy component markup from
`node_modules/signal-design/ai/components.json` (or `llms-full.txt`) rather than
inventing it.

Hard rules:
- Square corners: never `rounded-*` or `border-radius`.
- Flat: no blurred shadows, glow, glass or CSS gradients.
- Color only for status and focus, through roles (`data-tone="danger"`, `text-danger`);
  navigation, headings and icons stay black, white and grey.
- Tokens only (`var(--sd-*)`, `bg-surface`, `text-fg-muted`); never hex values.
- Source Code Pro 400/600 only.
- Motion only on state change, 120–200ms.
- Drive state with ARIA and `data-*` attributes; call `init()` from `signal-design/js`
  when markup uses `data-sd-*`.

Use the native element plus Signal for dialogs, popovers, tooltips, tabs and selects,
and `sd-shell` for app layout. Icon-only buttons need `aria-label`; each page needs one
`<h1>` and an `<a class="sd-skip" href="#main">` skip link.

Before finishing, run `npx signal-design check <url> --a11y` on the running page and
fix what it reports.
